  "caption": "Quinn took on a pickle jar and lost. After that, keys, pegs and texting all felt pinchy at the base of the thumb.\n\nThumb-base arthritis is common from the 50s and is often very manageable. How it looks on an X-ray often doesn't match how much it hurts.\n\nWhat can help: bigger handles and jar openers, carrying bags on your forearms or palms instead of in a pinch grip, sharing tasks between both hands, a fitted splint on heavy days, and gentle thumb-base strengthening. You don't have to give up hobbies like knitting — pacing and grip tweaks often help.\n\nIf pain persists despite these changes, see your GP, a physio or a hand therapist.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
